meta {
  name: Leave Game Session
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sessionId}}/leave
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{participantToken}}
}

tests {
  test("marks the learner as having left the Game Session", function() {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.state.sessionId).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/sessions/:sessionId/leave (`leaveGameSession`)

  Marks the calling learner (`{{participantToken}}`) as departed (`leftAt` timestamp set on the roster, `participantCount` decremented). Calling `leave` a second time is an idempotent `200 OK` no-op.

  Once a learner has left, read endpoints (`getGameSessionState`, `listRoundChains`, `getRoundStandings`) still succeed, while write endpoints (`submitConceptChain`, `adjudicateConceptChain`, `submitAssessmentAttempt`, `submitPerceptionSurvey`) refuse with `403 PARTICIPANT_HAS_LEFT`.

  ## Authentication
  - **`BearerAuth` (`role: "participant"`)**: `Authorization: Bearer {{participantToken}}`

  ## Responses & Error Codes (`ApiErrorCode`)
  - **`200 OK`**: `{ state: PublicSessionState }`
  - **`401 UNAUTHORIZED_TOKEN`**: Missing or invalid Capability Token.
  - **`403 FORBIDDEN_ROLE`**: Caller is an `instructor` (instructors use `POST /end` instead) or token belongs to another session.
  - **`404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND`**: Unknown `sessionId`.
}
